{"code":"5482KTB1Y","credits":5.00,"data":{"additional":{"values":[{"name":"language","subType":"EDUCATION_LANGUAGE","type":"ELEMENT","values":["ENG"]},{"name":"exchange","type":"BOOLEAN","values":["true"]},{"name":"studyguideLocation","subType":"StudyLocation","type":"REFERENCE","values":["L"]},{"name":"optional","type":"BOOLEAN","values":["true"]},{"name":"alacarte","type":"BOOLEAN","values":["true"]},{"name":"minorvak","type":"BOOLEAN","values":["true"]},{"name":"evening","type":"BOOLEAN","values":["false"]},{"name":"contract","type":"BOOLEAN","values":["true"]},{"name":"inclusion","type":"BOOLEAN","values":["false"]},{"name":"honours","type":"BOOLEAN","values":["false"]},{"name":"level","subType":"DIFFICULTY","type":"ELEMENT","values":["200"]},{"name":"loopbaan","subType":"loopbaanRef","type":"REFERENCE","values":["10"]}]},"assessments":[{"assessment":{"category":"E","code":"5482KTB1R","id":"267717","key":115751,"module":{"code":"5482KTB1Y","id":"267713","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Tantric Buddhism"},{"language":"NL","value":"Tantric Buddhism"}],"uid":"6626e6a1-98c2-467d-9b8b-000132da6a17"},"names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Tantric Buddhism"},{"language":"NL","value":"Tantric Buddhism"}],"type":"SCH","typeAbbreviation":"SCH","uid":"2ed1051f-6c0f-4571-ae57-e7ba8c389629","values":[{"name":"examDateFlag","type":"BOOLEAN","values":["true"]},{"name":"dynClassData","subType":"dynamicClassDataRef","type":"REFERENCE","values":["LEI0"]},{"name":"englishNameShort","type":"STRING","values":["Tantric Buddhism SCH"]},{"name":"PACC","type":"BOOLEAN","values":["true"]},{"name":"resit","subType":"StudieactAanmaken","type":"REFERENCE","values":["ScheduleY"]},{"name":"studiegidsnummerY","type":"STRING","values":["5482KTB1Y"]},{"name":"Toetsvorm","type":"STRING","values":["SCH"]},{"name":"exam","subType":"StudieactAanmaken","type":"REFERENCE","values":["ScheduleY"]},{"name":"dutchNameLong","type":"STRING","values":["Tantric Buddhism"]},{"name":"englishNameLong","type":"STRING","values":["Tantric Buddhism"]},{"name":"schedulePrint","subType":"yesNoReference","type":"REFERENCE","values":["Y"]},{"name":"gradingScale","subType":"gradingScaleRef","type":"REFERENCE","values":["GRD"]},{"name":"dutchNameShort","type":"STRING","values":["Tantric Buddhism SCH"]}],"year":{"code":"2026-2027","id":"2261","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"2026-2027"},{"language":"NL","value":"2026-2027"}],"uid":"07254806-916f-4cca-82a0-2e69a4a95e9f"}},"required":true,"values":[{"name":"evaluate","subType":"yesNoReference","type":"REFERENCE","values":["Y"]}],"weighting":1.00}],"capacity":{"optimum":15.00},"code":"5482KTB1Y","credits":{"optimum":5.00},"descriptions":[{"language":"EN","text":"From its birth in approximately the 4th c. BCE India; the Buddhist tradition grew over approximately two millenia until its ultimate destruction in India around the 13th c. The period of its Indian life saw the  continual production of new literature and the evolution of new practices. From around a millenium after its initial founding; a new stream began to develop within Mahāyāna traditions; which can retrospectively be termed Tantra. This tantric tradition generated an enormous scriptual; commentarial and practice-oriented literature; much of which remains unstudied; and motivated new material creations; including those related to maṇḍalas. Buddhist tantra became highly influential not only in India itself ; where it dominated the later centuries of the tradition; but also in Tibet; where it still survives; and in Indonesia. This course offers an introductory survey of tantric Buddhist traditions; with main focus on the Indian background; its literatures and practices; its interactions with; chiefly; Śaivite traditions; and some attention paid to its subsequent spread to Indonesia; to Tibet and to East Asia.","type":{"code":"CO","id":"CO","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Description"},{"language":"NL","value":"Beschrijving"}],"uid":"9b0c3e97-ad09-42d7-a5bb-afdaf6f1877f"}},{"language":"EN","text":"Reading list to be provided; no books are required for purchase; readings will be online through the library or provided on BrightSpace.","type":{"code":"LI","id":"LI","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Reading list"},{"language":"NL","value":"Literatuurlijst"}],"uid":"fbd93a9e-ca99-4bcc-807f-39235bb6000b"}},{"language":"EN","text":"Enrolment through [MyStudyMap](https://mijn.universiteitleiden.nl/login) is mandatory.\rGeneral information about course and exam enrolment is available on the [website](https://www.student.universiteitleiden.nl/en/your-study-programme/courses-and-exams/enrolment/humanities/english-language-and-culture-ba?cf=humanities&cd=french-language-and-culture-ba#tab-2).","type":{"code":"ENR","id":"ENR","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Registration"},{"language":"NL","value":"Inschrijven"}],"uid":"a77a2043-b0a9-450d-b780-1e90a4d3290c"}},{"language":"EN","text":"Students will develop abilities in close reading of secondary scholarship and of primary sources in translation; often with a comparative perspective in mind. They will thereby sharpen their critical eye in textual analysis. The materials are often challenging and demand of students flexibility of mind; the ability to openly consider alternative viewpoints; to listen openly to others; and to articulate their own perspectives on the material.","type":{"code":"LO","id":"LO","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Course objectives"},{"language":"NL","value":"Leerdoelen"}],"uid":"b54eb210-96e8-490d-aadb-a70571a665d9"}},{"language":"EN","text":"Background in the study of Buddhism would be a tremendous plus; for students without such background; the instructor will recommend important readings. Otherwise; the ability to communicate clearly in English is essential.","type":{"code":"AR","id":"AR","names":[{"language":"EN","value":"Admission requirements"},{"language":"NL","value":"Toegangseisen"}],"uid":"2c481598-5834-4422-a338-1eb346d6f52c"}},{"language":"EN","text":"* For su